          "pull_request": {
            "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/paulmillr/chokidar/pulls/1494",
            "html_url": "https://github.com/paulmillr/chokidar/pull/1494",
            "diff_url": "https://github.com/paulmillr/chokidar/pull/1494.diff",
            "patch_url": "https://github.com/paulmillr/chokidar/pull/1494.patch",
            "merged_at": null
          },
          "body": "When `cwd` makes a watched directory's key exactly `__proto__`, `getWatched()` invokes the inherited setter instead of creating an own property. The directory disappears from `Object.keys()` and JSON output, and the returned object's prototype becomes its child array.\n\nDefine each directory as an enumerable, writable, configurable own data property, preserving the existing `Object.prototype` return type and sorted child lists. Add real filesystem regressions for empty/nonempty `__proto__` directories with cwd and absolute paths, ordinary siblings, serialization, sorting and behavior after close. These tests run in the existing native, recursive-preferred and polling suites.\n\nFixes #1493.\n\nValidation on macOS / Node 22.22.3:\n- `npm ci`\n- `npm run build`\n- `npm test` — 461 tests passed\n- `JSBT_FILTER=getWatched npm test` — 18 tests passed; new regression failed before the fix\n- `npm pack --dry-run`\n- Prettier check for both changed files\n- CI's backend parity benchmark smoke configuration\n\nThe two-file diff also passed an independent review.\n",
